# Obsidian workspace state — rewritten constantly as you move panes around.
# Left tracked, every pane switch would auto-commit and trigger a deploy.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# Generated site output — rebuilt by CI on every push; never a source of truth.
.tracker-site/

# Obsidian's local trash and macOS cruft
.trash/
.DS_Store

# Retired Cloudflare Pages deploy. Its cache held an account id, account name and
# the old project name in a tracked file on a public repo; ignored so a future
# wrangler run cannot re-add them.
.wrangler/

# Raw source material dropped for /distill, and the originals it archives after
# ingesting them. This keeps the paste, its formatting and its original filename
# out of a public repo that auto-commits on a timer.
#
# It does NOT keep dump *content* private, and an earlier version of this comment
# wrongly implied it did. Brain/Nodes/ is tracked, and check.rb's FACTTEXT rule
# requires every atomic fact to appear in its node verbatim — so the content of a
# dump is published even though the dump file never is. Confidentiality is decided
# at drop time by whoever puts the file here. Nothing downstream redacts it.
Brain/_Dump/

# Source Ledgers, per operator decision 2026-08-16. The ledger's Anchor column is
# exact substrings of the dump, and it carries the removals log and undefined-terms
# apparatus, so it stays on this machine.
# The cost, accepted knowingly: a clone loses the losslessness audit trail. The
# Sources column of Brain — Index and every node's `sources:` link will not resolve
# for anyone else, and Obsidian renders an unresolved wikilink as plain text.
# .gitkeep stays tracked so the folder itself survives a clone.
Brain/_Sources/*
!Brain/_Sources/.gitkeep

# Temporary run digest. Gitignored on purpose: it carries the confidentiality
# analysis, the doctrine-vs-record divergence table and pre-announcement material.
# Delete this line to publish it.
tempfindings.md

# Decision sheet for the open calls the distiller cannot make. Same reason as the
# digest above: it names the pre-announcement sessions, quotes both sides of the
# doctrine-vs-record divergences, and restates the confidentiality posture.
# Delete this line to publish it.
decisions-open.md
